# Sets, set comprehensions, and inline records (B01+U3).
# The `{}` surface executes set literals, comprehensions with a guard,
# and path-prefixed record literals; `v in s` is the comparison-tier
# membership operator (ASCII for ∈), disjoint from the binder `in` (X13
# charter, language/reference/lexical-layout-and-source.md).
# Bare `{x: 1}` (record spelling without a path prefix) is ambiguous and is
# refused at parse time with E-SYN-154 (tests/invalid/r3_sets_tub8_ambiguous.emath).
emath function SetsAndRecords:
    definitions:
        pair = {2, 3, 5}
        tens = {n in 0..100 if n >= 90}
        two_in_tens = 2 in tens
        origin = Point:{x: 0.0, y: 0.0}
